{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Aeon Rend makes Chromatic Shard strike again (#718)",
  "contract": "Aeon Rend 583248 applies aura 42 (proc trigger spell) twice - on Chromatic Shard 801292 itself (\"strike again\") and on 583247, whose SPELL_EFFECT_ASCENSION_RESET_COOLDOWN clears 801292's cooldown - but Spell.dbc gives 583248 ProcFlags 0, so SpellMgr::LoadSpellProcs generated no entry and Aura::GetProcEffectMask returned 0 for every event. Its tooltip is \"Your Chromatic Shard now has a $h% chance to strike again and incur no cooldown\", with $h = the record's own ProcChance of 25, and Aura::GetProcEffectMask rolls that chance once per event for both effects together. The scenario counts the re-strikes with spell_proc_count, which reports how many spells the aura fired as their named trigger, rather than weighing the dummy's health: a health measurement needs every cast of a volley to land, and on this harness they do not. Measured on this tree, a 25-cast volley delivered 7166 damage at about 440 per critical hit - roughly sixteen casts, two thirds of what was submitted. Chromatic Shard carries CategoryRecoveryTime 30000, cleared per cast by fixturing the class's own Incarnation of Chaos buff 504723 (aura 108, MiscValue 11 = SPELLMOD_COOLDOWN, -100%, class-masked to Chromatic Shard's SpellFamilyFlags word1 4096); Player::AddSpellAndCategoryCooldowns applies SPELLMOD_COOLDOWN to catrec as well as rec, but the harness' set_aura does not report whether the buff actually reapplied, and a cast that meets the full category cooldown is rejected outright. A rejected cast costs the count nothing, so the assertion asks only for at least one re-strike out of forty casts: at the observed two thirds landing rate that is 0.75^26 = 0.07%, and even if only half of them landed it would be 0.75^20 = 0.3%. Before the volley the same counter must read zero, which is the state this issue reported: with no spell_proc row, Aura::GetProcEffectMask returns 0 for every event and the talent never fires. The fixture creature is a critter template (Dig Rat 3444, creature_template.type 8) rather than a levelled mob, and the scenario pins neither its level nor a maximum health it expects the server to produce. AscensionCompat's CanScaleCreature (AscensionCompat.cpp:6093-6099) excludes critters from local level scaling, so this fixture keeps the maximum health CoAGameplayTest asked for instead of having it rebuilt by Creature::SelectLevel, which on this tree leaves a levelled creature 36 at level 16 with 349 maximum health - not enough to survive a volley, and not a number a scenario may depend on, since upstream retunes it. Chromatic Shard's CastingTimeIndex 22 is 3500 ms (SpellCastTimes.dbc), so the casts are spaced 4500 ms. The count is a count of triggered spells, not of procs: Aeon Rend's two aura-42 effects fire together, so one roll records both 801292 and 583247 against this aura. The observed 14 over forty casts is therefore about seven rolls out of roughly twenty-eight landed casts, which is the record's 25%. The assertion asks only for one, so the factor does not matter to it.",
  "timeout_ms": 300000,
